From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] live in-world panel images

The owner asked for status on the panel itself, not only a full-screen console. Only the renderer can
overwrite a texture, so this adds one capability: gi.RemapShader (already in the renderer, now routed
through the SP bridge) and gi.UpdatePanelImage, which finds a named shader's base image and uploads
32-bit RGBA into it (resampling to the image's own size, Vulkan via vk_upload_image_data with the
update flag). The game decides what to draw and when; with the module unset the two import slots are
null and nothing changes. Everything the panel shows is in module/ship/lwh_panel.cpp.
---
diff --git a/efgame/src/game/g_public.h b/efgame/src/game/g_public.h
--- a/efgame/src/game/g_public.h
+++ b/efgame/src/game/g_public.h
@@ -201,6 +201,13 @@
 	// dynamic memory allocator for things that need to be freed
 	void	*(*Malloc)( int bytes );
 	void	(*Free)( void *buf );
+
+	// Long Way Home: a world surface can show state the game recomputes. RemapShader points a
+	// texture name at a shader, and UpdatePanelImage overwrites that shader's base image with the
+	// game's live 32-bit RGBA. Both are engine capabilities; the game decides what to draw and
+	// calls them only while its simulation runs.
+	void	(*RemapShader)( const char *oldShader, const char *newShader, const char *offsetTime );
+	void	(*UpdatePanelImage)( const char *shaderName, const byte *rgba, int width, int height );
 } game_import_t;
 
